the people who want to take things away, there tends to be sort of one advocate for it. And one of the things that we focus on in organizational life is that people who lead more large and complex systems and make life difficult for all of us, those are the people who tend to get rewarded, not the people who take things away. Just as an example, in my own university and I suspect many other organizations in the world, a good way if you're a manager to get a raise is to build a larger and larger organization because the more people
