00:38:20.000 --> 00:39:01.000
about how each part works to sort of glue the system together and to serve as tour guides for all of us. You talk about a very interesting idea called the rule of halves. What is the rule of halves, Bob? So the rule of halves, this is an idea that actually Lydie Klotz, he and I came up with the notion that as sort of a thought experiment, if you went through the number of meetings you have, the length of the emails, the number of emails you sent, what would happen if you cut it by 50%? And then the example we use in the book comes to us from a guy named Rob Cross.
